   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Avoir mal à»",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something hurts, use **avoir mal à** + body part.",
      "With **à**, use **à la** (feminine), **au** (masculine) or **aux** (plural): **J'ai mal à la tête** (I have a headache), **J'ai mal au ventre** (I have a stomach ache), **J'ai mal aux pieds** (my feet hurt)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out for the article",
     "texto": [
      "In French, parts of the body take the article, not «my», unlike in English: **la tête**, **le ventre**, **les pieds**. You don't say «my» with these parts: **J'ai mal à la tête**, not «j'ai mal à ma tête»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
